So what happens if a system ignores the red light?

19:24.980 --> 19:39.120
If an AI system ignores this mathematical warning and forces the context together anyway to satisfy a prompt, it experiences a global hallucination. The individual parts make sense locally, but the whole is a monster.

19:39.120 --> 19:48.080
So a hallucination isn't necessarily generating fake things from scratch. Sometimes it's taking two very real things and gluing them together in a way that violates physics.

19:48.240 --> 19:48.680
Exactly.

19:48.940 --> 19:58.860
So how do we fix it? How does the system ensure the red light stays off? The paper introduces an architecture called CLIO, right? Cognitive Loop via In-Situ Optimization.

19:58.860 --> 20:09.580
Yes. CLIO models cognition as a continuous recursive loop. You perceive data, you predict what it means, you act on it, and then you perceive the result of your action.

20:10.060 --> 20:19.240
But mathematically, CLIO is doing something very specific to avoid those stitching errors. It is performing a gradient descent on what is called a Morse potential.

20:19.240 --> 20:21.560
Okay, let's visualize this Morse potential.

20:21.860 --> 20:36.920
Imagine the manifold, the landscape of reality, is a physical terrain with steep hills and deep valleys. The valleys are stable, coherent, semantic states. They are places where all your contexts glue together perfectly, where the panorama photo stitches flawlessly.

20:37.080 --> 20:38.080
Got it. Valleys are good.

20:38.480 --> 20:47.400
The hills, on the other hand, are regions of high inconsistency. They are the three-headed dogs. CLIO is essentially a ball rolling on this landscape.

20:47.400 --> 21:01.700
When it encounters a stitching error, it is pushed up a hill. But gravity, in this case, the mathematical optimization process, constantly pulls the ball down the slope, correcting its trajectory, rolling it back down until it settles safely into a valley of coherent meaning.

21:01.700 --> 21:07.060
Wait, let me stop you there. This is a massive philosophical claim. Mask as math.

21:08.100 --> 21:17.080
Are we saying that human cognition, the act of thinking, reasoning, perceiving the world, is literally just a mathematical error correction mechanism?

21:17.080 --> 21:26.800
Under this framework, yes. That is exactly what it is. The text connects this directly to the free energy principle in neuroscience, which was pioneered by Carl Fristen.

21:27.440 --> 21:31.200
The idea that the brain is essentially just an engine designed to minimize surprise.

21:31.380 --> 21:40.360
Correct. Active inference, the way we constantly interact with the world to update our beliefs and minimize prediction errors, is described here as geodesic control.

21:40.800 --> 21:41.640
Geodesic control.

21:41.640 --> 21:46.300
Yes. A geodesic is the shortest, smoothest possible path on a curved surface.

21:46.900 --> 21:56.420
So your brain is constantly, actively moving along the manifold, feeling out the terrain, seeking the smoothest path that keeps all your sensory and linguistic context perfectly glued together.

21:57.120 --> 21:59.500
Thinking is simply the geometry of staying on the manifold.

21:59.500 --> 22:04.720
That is mind-bending. Our brains aren't these magical, ethereal consciousness machines.

22:05.260 --> 22:12.800
They're just physical systems rolling down hills, desperately trying to find the smoothest path across the paper without falling off into the noise.

22:12.960 --> 22:14.920
It is a very mechanistic view, yes.

22:15.140 --> 22:19.340
But this leads us to a really unsettling problem. What if the stitching is seamless?

22:19.700 --> 22:29.360
What if the panorama photo looks flawless, and every single step you take makes perfect logical sense, but the entire system is still somehow completely wrong?

22:29.360 --> 22:33.820
This is perhaps the most insidious type of hallucination identified in the framework.

22:34.660 --> 22:40.340
It's a phenomenon called semantic drift, and it is governed by a principle called Levi-Savita transport.

22:40.780 --> 22:44.480
Okay, Levi-Savita transport. Break down the physical intuition for me.

22:44.660 --> 22:50.160
To understand this, we have to remember that our manifold, our piece of paper, is not perfectly flat.

22:50.580 --> 22:53.620
It is curved and folded in highly complex ways.

22:54.300 --> 23:03.060
Levi-Savita transport is the mathematical rule for how you move a vector, like an arrow pointing in a specific direction, along a curved space while keeping it locally straight.

23:03.300 --> 23:04.640
Locally straight, but globally.

23:05.020 --> 23:05.580
Exactly.

23:05.580 --> 23:12.440
When you navigate a highly curved manifold, you can follow the rules perfectly at every single local step.

23:12.940 --> 23:15.940
You keep your arrow pointing straight ahead relative to your feet.

23:16.400 --> 23:26.680
But because the space itself is curved beneath you, if you follow a closed loop and return to the exact spot where you started, your area will be pointing in a completely different direction.

23:26.680 --> 23:30.180
The classic analogy for this is walking on the surface of the Earth.

23:30.660 --> 23:34.880
Imagine you are standing exactly on the equator facing due north.

23:35.160 --> 23:36.320
You have a compass in your hand.

23:36.680 --> 23:40.040
You walk perfectly straight north until you hit the North Pole.

23:40.280 --> 23:41.260
Okay, you're at the North Pole.

23:41.440 --> 23:47.240
Then you stop and you turn exactly 90 degrees to your right, so now you are facing east.

23:47.500 --> 23:50.320
You walk perfectly straight down until you hit the equator again.

23:50.320 --> 23:57.840
Finally, you stop, turn 90 degrees to your right again, and walk straight west along the equator back to your exact starting point.

23:57.900 --> 23:58.920
So you've made a triangle.

23:59.100 --> 23:59.520
Exactly.

23:59.680 --> 23:59.840
Yeah.

23:59.980 --> 24:01.000
Now think about what just happened.

24:01.580 --> 24:05.440
Every single step you took was perfectly straight within your local perspective.

24:05.800 --> 24:06.540
You didn't zigzag.

24:06.900 --> 24:09.060
You only made precise 90 degree turns.

24:09.700 --> 24:11.340
The local logic was flawless.

24:11.620 --> 24:12.100
Flawless.

24:12.100 --> 24:16.680
But when you arrive back at your starting point, you are no longer facing north.

24:16.680 --> 24:20.320
You are facing south or east, depending on your path.

24:20.520 --> 24:27.680
Because the Earth is a sphere, your frame of reference rotated entirely, even though you never explicitly rotated it yourself.

24:27.880 --> 24:31.520
That is a flawless explanation of what mathematicians call holonomy.

24:31.980 --> 24:36.820
You experienced a global rotation purely through local straight line movement.

24:36.960 --> 24:37.520
Holonomy.

24:37.620 --> 24:37.880
Yes.

24:37.880 --> 24:47.660
Now, if we scale this up and apply it to semantic spaces, to the realm of ideas, beliefs, and narratives, think about what this implies.

24:48.500 --> 24:50.760
Think about fragmented media echo chambers.

24:51.320 --> 24:55.940
Think about deeply entrenched institutional policy cycles or political polarization.

24:56.420 --> 24:56.820
Oh, wow.

24:57.020 --> 24:58.040
Okay, I see where this is going.

24:58.160 --> 25:03.400
You can have a group of people or an entire political faction following a perfectly logical local narrative.

25:03.640 --> 25:07.120
Every news article they read confirms the logic of the last one.

25:07.120 --> 25:11.500
Every policy decision logically follows the metric established by the previous decision.

25:11.700 --> 25:14.800
They are taking perfectly straight steps on their semantic manifold.

25:14.980 --> 25:16.180
But their manifold is curved.

25:16.480 --> 25:16.780
Right.

25:17.000 --> 25:27.260
Because their specific cultural or media manifold is highly curved by specific biases, selective reporting, or algorithmic feeds, they travel in a loop.

25:27.260 --> 25:38.380
Years later, they end up with a global worldview that is entirely rotated, completely incompatible with the worldview of someone navigating a differently curved part of the manifold.

25:38.380 --> 25:43.740
And it's crucial to point out here, for you listening, that this geometry applies neutrally to everyone.

25:44.520 --> 25:48.700
This isn't about one political faction being right and another being wrong or hallucinating.

25:49.140 --> 25:50.580
The math doesn't take sides.

25:51.000 --> 25:52.380
It is completely agnostic.

25:52.600 --> 25:52.960
Absolutely.

25:53.380 --> 25:57.960
The terrifying part is that the math shows that both sides can be internally, locally consistent.

25:58.540 --> 26:00.420
They are both doing the math right locally.

26:00.760 --> 26:02.540
Every step they take makes sense to them.

26:02.540 --> 26:07.640
But because they are trapped in different curved loops, they become globally misaligned.

26:07.840 --> 26:12.660
They literally cannot understand each other because their coordinate systems have rotated away from one another.

26:12.780 --> 26:16.700
A straight line for one group looks like a violent curve to the other.

26:16.840 --> 26:17.380
Precisely.

26:17.840 --> 26:21.020
It is a failure of global transport, not local logic.

26:21.020 --> 26:29.960
And this accumulated holonomy, the slow, invisible drift of orientation, is far harder to detect and correct than a simple factual error.

26:30.280 --> 26:30.840
Why is that?

26:31.600 --> 26:35.480
Well, if you make a factual error, the obstruction class flashes red.

26:35.940 --> 26:37.500
The panorama photo stitch is wrong.

26:37.720 --> 26:39.660
You see the three-headed dog and you fix it.

26:39.960 --> 26:41.940
But with holonomy, there is no red light.

26:42.460 --> 26:46.660
Every individual step feels completely true and rigorous to the person taking it.

26:46.660 --> 26:50.940
But the hallucination is only visible from a global bird's-eye perspective.

26:51.360 --> 26:53.160
Which brings us to a really scary question.

26:53.480 --> 26:55.800
We've talked about smoothly drifting on the manifold.

26:56.000 --> 26:57.340
We've talked about rolling down hills.

26:57.860 --> 27:00.240
But what happens when the curvature is too extreme?

27:00.680 --> 27:04.340
What happens when the stress is too much and the manifold itself breaks?

27:04.780 --> 27:08.440
That brings us to semantic phase transitions and singularities.

27:08.440 --> 27:17.300
The Morse-theoretic flow we talked about, that comforting process of rolling smoothly down into a valley of meaning, works great when the manifold is stable and slowly changing.

27:17.480 --> 27:18.500
But things aren't always stable.

27:18.820 --> 27:19.040
Right.

27:19.800 --> 27:31.340
Real systems, whether they are individual human minds, scientific communities, or financial markets, sometimes face conditions where the curvature of the manifold accumulates faster than the system can adapt to it.

27:31.600 --> 27:32.900
Give me a mechanism for that.

27:33.380 --> 27:34.600
How does curvature accumulate?

27:34.720 --> 27:38.260
It happens through rapid, contradictory update pressures.

27:38.960 --> 27:41.360
Imagine an influx of anomalous data.

27:41.860 --> 27:46.480
Stuff that completely defies your current understanding of the world but is undeniably real.

27:46.820 --> 27:51.040
Your brain tries to stitch it into your existing context, but the overlap is wrong.

27:51.160 --> 27:52.100
The red light is flashing.

27:52.460 --> 27:52.720
Yes.

27:53.080 --> 27:54.520
The obstruction class rises.

27:55.040 --> 27:58.060
You try to force it, and the conceptual space begins to warp.

27:58.060 --> 28:03.980
When this pressure becomes too high, the curvature at a specific point on the manifold approaches infinity.

28:04.460 --> 28:05.940
Curvature approaching infinity.

28:06.120 --> 28:07.160
That sounds like a black hole.

28:07.160 --> 28:08.500
That sounds catastrophic.

28:08.500 --> 28:10.880
It is a topological bifurcation.

28:11.580 --> 28:12.880
A singularity forms.

28:13.460 --> 28:15.660
The smooth geometry breaks down completely.

28:16.120 --> 28:17.820
The tangent spaces become ambiguous.

28:18.160 --> 28:21.040
Remember that comforting valley of meaning we were rolling into?

28:21.720 --> 28:25.480
Suddenly that valley splits violently into two incompatible basings.

28:25.960 --> 28:30.740
Or, conversely, previously distinct concepts suddenly collapse into one chaotic mess.

28:30.740 --> 28:34.460
The system experiences a semantic phase transition.

28:34.460 --> 28:37.040
Wait, I need an example of a semantic phase transition.

28:37.420 --> 28:40.860
What does a topological bifurcation look like in the real world?

28:41.240 --> 28:44.180
Are we talking about a society collapsing or someone having a nervous breakdown?

28:44.540 --> 28:45.460
Both, fundamentally.

28:46.000 --> 28:48.740
On a macro scale, think about a paradigm shift in science.

28:48.920 --> 28:52.980
For decades, physicists operated comfortably on the manifold of Newtonian mechanics.

28:52.980 --> 28:55.840
It was a massive, highly stable valley of meaning.

28:56.400 --> 28:58.840
It explained apples falling and planets orbiting.

28:59.040 --> 29:00.320
It worked for everyday life.

29:00.540 --> 29:01.060
It did.

29:01.560 --> 29:09.560
But then, in the late 19th and early 20th centuries, anomalous observations about the speed of light and electromagnetism started piling up.

29:09.560 --> 29:11.840
These were contradictory updates.

29:12.540 --> 29:15.780
The curvature of the Newtonian manifold grew and grew.

29:16.380 --> 29:22.020
Scientists tried to patch it with theories like the luminiferous ether, which was just adding normal direction noise.

29:22.260 --> 29:23.420
Trying to map the void again.

29:23.480 --> 29:23.960
Exactly.

29:24.700 --> 29:26.560
Eventually, the curvature hit infinity.

29:26.920 --> 29:27.380
It broke.

29:27.700 --> 29:30.340
The entire conceptual framework dissolved abruptly.

29:30.780 --> 29:34.840
And the manifold bifurcated into general relativity and quantum mechanics.

29:34.960 --> 29:35.900
And on a personal level.

29:36.400 --> 29:38.560
Think about a profound personal crisis.

29:38.560 --> 29:42.880
A sudden betrayal by a spouse or an unexpected loss.

29:43.340 --> 29:50.300
The foundational rules you use to navigate your daily life, your personal manifold, suddenly cannot accommodate the new reality.

29:50.680 --> 29:52.600
Your conceptual framework dissolves.

29:52.660 --> 29:53.520
It's devastating.

29:53.660 --> 29:54.700
You don't just feel sad.

29:54.740 --> 29:57.500
You feel like the physical world literally doesn't make sense anymore.

29:57.780 --> 29:59.220
Your manifold had fractured.

29:59.460 --> 30:02.240
You don't know how to move forward because the tangent space is shattered.

30:02.620 --> 30:02.960
Wow.

30:03.840 --> 30:05.320
That is incredibly heavy.

30:05.320 --> 30:09.140
But it makes so much sense of that feeling of profound disorientation.

30:09.420 --> 30:11.280
So how does the system survive that?

30:11.540 --> 30:14.580
Does the math offer a way to heal a broken manifold?

30:15.100 --> 30:15.540
It does.

30:15.680 --> 30:17.500
It introduces the concept of Ricci flow.

30:17.700 --> 30:18.280
Ricci flow.

30:18.400 --> 30:18.580
Okay.

30:18.700 --> 30:19.580
Break that down for me.

30:19.940 --> 30:26.880
In differential geometry, Ricci flow is a process that evolves the metric of a space over time to smooth out its curvature.

30:27.880 --> 30:32.820
Imagine a piece of metal with a lot of structural stress concentrated in one sharp point.

30:32.820 --> 30:33.220
Okay.

30:33.320 --> 30:34.200
Like a bent wire.

30:34.360 --> 30:34.660
Yes.

30:35.380 --> 30:42.100
If you heat the metal, the heat diffuses through the material, spreading out the stress and smoothing the sharp point into a gentle curve.

30:42.100 --> 30:50.600
In a cognitive or social system, implementing Ricci flow means actively engaging in conceptual restructuring before the pressure reaches infinity.

30:50.860 --> 30:52.160
So you have to bend before you break.

30:52.260 --> 30:52.800
Precisely.

30:52.800 --> 30:59.280
It means sacrificing some of your rigid, local precision to maintain the global connectivity of your worldview.

30:59.920 --> 31:05.600
It's the mathematical equivalent of cognitive flexibility or forgiveness or scientific open-mindedness.

31:05.960 --> 31:08.680
You let the heat diffuse so the structure doesn't snap.

31:08.960 --> 31:10.340
Let's scale this up even further.

31:10.800 --> 31:11.840
We've looked at AI.

31:12.300 --> 31:16.180
We've looked at personal psychological crises and scientific revolutions.

31:16.180 --> 31:19.180
Now, let's apply this directly to human society.

31:20.000 --> 31:25.240
How do our massive institutions, like our schools, our corporations, our governments, hallucinate?

31:25.520 --> 31:28.560
They hallucinate by fundamentally misunderstanding statistics.

31:29.120 --> 31:35.180
Specifically, they commit a geometric error by confusing statistical rarity with ambient noise.

31:35.380 --> 31:36.200
This is fascinating.

31:36.300 --> 31:37.600
Let's break down the myth of the normal.

31:37.600 --> 31:47.360
If you take a large population of people and measure 10 different dimensions, let's say height, reading speed, extroversion, sleep needs, mathematical aptitude, and so on,

31:47.800 --> 31:53.040
and you try to find someone who is exactly the statistical average in all 10 categories.

31:53.080 --> 31:53.760
You won't find them.

31:53.820 --> 31:54.180
Exactly.

31:54.320 --> 31:55.640
You will find exactly zero people.

31:55.900 --> 31:58.280
The mean, the average person is a statistical ghost.

31:58.940 --> 32:06.220
Yet our institutions design all their rules, their physical spaces, their work hours, and their performance metrics for this phantom average.

32:06.220 --> 32:12.520
And the framework defines this as social hallucination in a very precise geometric sense.

32:13.340 --> 32:16.680
Think about a normal distribution, a classic bell curve.

32:17.200 --> 32:20.600
A bell curve does not assert a moral or geometric hierarchy.

32:20.860 --> 32:23.220
It purely describes population density.

32:23.580 --> 32:24.380
How many people are aware?

32:24.540 --> 32:24.740
Right.

32:25.000 --> 32:30.300
The mode, the peak of the bell curve in the middle, is just the most frequently occurring configuration.

32:30.640 --> 32:35.860
The tails of the bell curve, the extreme outliers on the left and right, are less frequent.

32:36.220 --> 32:42.100
But, and this is the critical, absolute center of the argument, they are still on the manifold.

32:42.380 --> 32:44.860
A seven foot tall person isn't a glitch in physics.

32:45.000 --> 32:45.820
They aren't a mistake.

32:46.060 --> 32:46.920
They're just rare.

32:47.400 --> 32:49.740
But they are completely structurally valid.

32:50.000 --> 32:50.540
Exactly.

32:50.960 --> 32:53.580
They possess fully lawful geometric structure.

32:54.100 --> 32:58.720
But when a bureaucracy designs a proxy metric tailored only for the statistical mean,

32:59.040 --> 33:02.080
and then forces everyone in the population to conform to it,

33:02.420 --> 33:05.080
it is applying a mathematical normal direction for them.

33:05.080 --> 33:06.060
It's pushing them off the paper.

33:06.060 --> 33:06.740
Yes.

33:07.140 --> 33:13.180
It is explicitly forcing real, highly diverse people to suppress their unique,

33:13.600 --> 33:18.240
geometrically valid dimensions in order to mimic a non-existent center.

33:18.620 --> 33:22.920
It is driving the population off its intrinsic manifold and into the void.

33:23.180 --> 33:25.980
If you are listening to this right now, think about your own life.

33:26.640 --> 33:32.360
Have you ever sat in a corporate performance review feeling like the rigid metrics they use to evaluate you

33:32.360 --> 33:37.440
are completely detached from your actual skills and the unique value you bring to the team?

33:37.680 --> 33:39.820
Or felt forced to be someone else.

33:39.820 --> 33:40.500
Yeah, exactly.

33:40.500 --> 33:47.140
Have you ever felt like you had to shrink yourself or fake a certain personality type just to survive the culture of a bureaucracy?

33:47.140 --> 33:51.420
If so, you were experiencing social hallucination firsthand.

33:51.920 --> 33:56.300
The institution was looking at you and labeling you as noise because you didn't fit the average.

33:56.460 --> 33:57.300
But you aren't noise.

33:57.500 --> 33:57.760
Right.

33:57.880 --> 33:58.700
You are not an error.

33:58.820 --> 34:02.260
You are just operating in a sparse, less populated region of the human manifold.

34:02.260 --> 34:04.740
Your trajectory is completely valid.

34:05.100 --> 34:09.920
The institution is the one hallucinating by trying to force you off the paper into empty space.

34:10.440 --> 34:17.480
It is a profound, mathematically rigorous validation of neurodiversity, physical variation, and systemic diversity.

34:18.120 --> 34:21.620
Compressing everyone toward the mean doesn't make a society more efficient.

34:22.200 --> 34:24.860
It actively destroys structural information.

34:25.380 --> 34:28.780
It reduces the representational capacity of the entire society.

34:28.780 --> 34:33.740
It is the societal equivalent of training an AI to predict noise.

34:33.980 --> 34:38.420
Okay, so society pushes us off the manifold using bad statistics and bureaucracy.

34:38.960 --> 34:44.380
But the framework argues that our own language tricks us into stepping off the manifold using grammar.

34:44.940 --> 34:47.740
This is the realm of language traps and category errors.

34:48.000 --> 34:52.360
This is an incredibly elegant application of the framework to linguistics and philosophy.

34:52.680 --> 34:56.240
We have this deep-seated assumption that if a sentence is grammatically correct,

34:56.240 --> 35:00.520
if it follows the rules of syntax, it must possess some kind of inherent meaning.

35:00.840 --> 35:02.520
It sounds right, so it must be right.

35:02.620 --> 35:02.980
Exactly.

35:03.340 --> 35:07.280
But the geometry shows that category errors are not just factual mistakes.

35:07.400 --> 35:11.580
They are attempts to navigate semantic spaces that have no lawful structure whatsoever.

35:11.940 --> 35:15.220
Let's use the classic paradox the text brings up to illustrate this.

35:15.720 --> 35:16.720
The age-old riddle.

35:17.420 --> 35:21.140
What happens when an unstoppable force meets an immovable object?

35:21.140 --> 35:25.620
You hear that, and your brain instantly gears up to try and solve it.

35:26.160 --> 35:29.220
It feels like a deep, profound, philosophical puzzle.

35:29.600 --> 35:31.760
It feels profound because it has perfect grammar.

35:32.100 --> 35:33.300
The syntax is flawless.

35:33.680 --> 35:35.780
You have a subject, a verb, and an object.

35:36.320 --> 35:38.920
But geometrically, it has zero structure.

35:39.620 --> 35:45.420
The definitions of unstoppable force and immovable object are mutually exclusive by their very nature.

35:45.760 --> 35:49.520
They constrain the manifold in ways that fundamentally cannot intersect.

35:49.520 --> 35:54.300
Right. If a force is truly unstoppable, then by definition, nothing in that universe can be immovable.

35:54.740 --> 35:55.320
And vice versa.

35:55.640 --> 35:56.060
Exactly.

35:56.580 --> 36:01.780
If you try to find the mathematical intersection of those two concepts, the resulting set is strictly empty.

36:02.020 --> 36:02.760
It doesn't exist.

36:03.180 --> 36:07.240
So when you spend time trying to answer that question, you are not doing deep philosophy.

36:07.860 --> 36:15.060
You are attempting to navigate a coordinate in the ambient space that has no corresponding reality on the semantic manifold.

36:15.200 --> 36:16.620
You are drawing in the air again.

36:16.980 --> 36:19.120
You are staring into the empty room and trying to map it.

36:19.120 --> 36:20.000
Precisely.

36:20.460 --> 36:25.580
And this mechanical insight explains one of the most dangerous flaws in large language models today.

36:26.300 --> 36:31.380
Language allows for what mathematicians call smooth interpolation through empty space.

36:31.560 --> 36:32.740
Smooth interpolation.

36:32.820 --> 36:33.120
Yes.

36:33.620 --> 36:40.220
Because an LLM like ChatGPT is trained on syntax, grammar, and the statistical proximity of words to one another,

36:40.220 --> 36:46.020
it can smoothly connect concepts that have absolutely no geometric or logical relationship in reality.

36:46.180 --> 36:47.500
Wait, let me make sure I'm getting this.

36:47.580 --> 36:52.940
Are you saying that fluency, the ability to speak smoothly and grammatically, is actually a trap?

36:52.940 --> 36:53.620
Absolutely.

36:53.620 --> 36:58.180
Fluency without geometric constraint is the exact definition of generating noise.

36:58.820 --> 37:06.220
An LLM will confidently generate a beautifully written, grammatically flawless, highly persuasive five-page essay

37:06.220 --> 37:10.800
explaining exactly what happens when an unstoppable force meets an immovable object.

37:11.200 --> 37:12.360
It will cite fake physics.

37:12.500 --> 37:13.900
It will sound entirely reasonable.

37:14.160 --> 37:15.000
But it's total nonsense.

37:15.000 --> 37:19.960
It is a pure, unadulterated hallucination because it is traversing a non-existent manifold.

37:20.520 --> 37:25.480
The local smoothness of the grammar completely masks the global incoherence of the logic.

37:25.820 --> 37:26.880
That is terrifying.

37:27.020 --> 37:31.380
When you think about how much we are starting to rely on these language models for truth,

37:31.600 --> 37:36.460
for medical advice, for legal summaries, we are biologically wired to trust fluency.

37:37.300 --> 37:41.300
When someone speaks confidently and grammatically, we assume they are on the manifold,

37:41.700 --> 37:44.460
but the AI is just smoothly gliding through the void.

37:44.460 --> 37:46.180
And that leads to a much bigger issue.

37:46.440 --> 37:46.620
Right.

37:46.780 --> 37:49.920
If language models can be tricked into generating smooth nonsense,

37:50.480 --> 37:55.000
