and only cares about optimizing their standardized test scores?

40:16.180 --> 40:17.460
That's a perfect example.

40:17.580 --> 40:21.680
The test was supposed to be a proxy for learning, but eventually learning the test becomes the entire goal.

40:21.680 --> 40:24.180
Yes, that is projection collapse in education.

40:24.520 --> 40:30.580
The school optimizes for the proxy, but the proxy cannot see the invisible dimension of actual student curiosity,

40:30.920 --> 40:33.700
so the system naturally accelerates into those blind spots.

40:33.820 --> 40:36.280
It destroys the curiosity to maximize the score.

