On a macro level, think of the global economy.

40:39.340 --> 40:40.400
Think of financial derivatives.

40:40.400 --> 40:47.580
They started as a way to represent and hedge the risk of actual material production, like farming or housing.

40:48.040 --> 40:48.640
That's a proxy.

40:49.540 --> 40:53.620
But then financial institutions created derivatives of those derivatives,

40:53.900 --> 40:59.580
and algorithms began optimizing trading purely for symbolic financial return at microsecond speeds.

40:59.720 --> 41:01.300
Detaching completely from reality.

41:01.460 --> 41:01.720
Yes.

